    <problem>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, \(f\), of the number of days, \(d\), since the epidemic began. The equation \(f(d)=50 \cdot (\frac{3}{2})^d\) defines \(f\).
          <br/><br/>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
            <item> How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.9.2. </para>
